# Allowed `tsc -b --noEmit` error count. Enforced by typecheck_frontend in
# scripts/_common.sh: the deploy fails above this number.
#
# Until 2026-08-08 the deploy gate ran bare `tsc --noEmit` against a
# solution-style tsconfig, which follows no references and so typechecked
# nothing at all. 199 errors accumulated behind that. This is what is left.
#
# The remaining one is not a type problem to paper over. usePayAndMintSuiNFT
# reads a "supplyLimitId" network variable that has never existed in
# suiNetworkConfig, so `tx.object(supplyLimitId)` in the Genesis NFT mint could
# never have worked. Its whole subtree is unreachable: NFTTierSection has no
# importers, PayAndMintNftCard is imported only by it, and pages/GenesisNftPage
# is referenced only from a commented-out route. Deleting it is the fix, and it
# wants the same before/after bundle check the protocol and wave1 trees got —
# note the live /dev/genesis-nft route mounts a *different* component
# (sections/genesis-nft/GenesisNftPage), so the two must not be conflated.
#
# Lower this in the same commit that fixes errors. The helper prints the real
# count and tells you when this can come down; it deliberately never edits this
# file itself, because a self-lowering baseline hides the progress it measures.
#
# Cleanup plan: .claude/handoffs/2026-08-08-nasun-website-tsc-gate.md
